## Agent process

### Issue tracker

Issues live in {{tracker.name}}; code and CI on {{platform.host}} ({{platform.url}}). Every tracker and CI action has one command, listed by name in the **Operations** table of `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`, which also covers the board, phases and releases.

### Triage labels

`needs-triage`, `needs-info`, `ready-for-agent`, `ready-for-human`, `wontfix`, plus `idea`. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`. Only {{tracker.ready_for_agent_by}} apply `ready-for-agent`.

### Domain docs

{{docs.contexts_line}} See `docs/agents/domain.md`.

### Repo profile

How to check, build and publish this repo, and what agents must not do here: `docs/agents/repo-profile.md`. Its **Checks** section is what the implementer and checks agents run. Full suites run in CI on every MR/PR; locally, run only the checks and tests that cover the change.

### Conventions

- Branches: `{{conventions.branch}}`. Commits: {{conventions.commits_line}}.
- Agents may {{agents.autonomy_line}}. Agents never merge, release, publish or deploy.

<!-- economy:start (left out when agents.economy is false) -->
## Working economically

- **One issue per conversation.** When an issue's MR/PR is open or a milestone is closed, stop and give a two- or three-line handoff so the session can be cleared.
- **Delegate routine work to cheaper agents** (`shipwright` plugin):
  - `implementer` ({{agents.models.implementer}}) for clearly specified code changes. The main conversation shapes the change and writes the plan.
  - `checks` ({{agents.models.checks}}) to run checks or watch a pipeline once, instead of polling.
  - `chores` ({{agents.models.chores}}) for board, label, milestone and release-notes bookkeeping.

  Do tiny edits inline: a spawned agent starts cold, so it only pays off for real work or noisy output.
- Read only the parts of files you need; grep before reading. Filter command output to the lines that matter. Keep replies short. Follow narrow asks literally.
<!-- economy:end -->

## Hard rules

- Gate every verify-then-commit step on **exit codes**, never on `| tail` output (a piped tail exits 0 and hides failures). State test counts only from the branch actually tested.
- After a routine merge, confirm it landed on the default branch and stop; don't poll deploy pipelines unless the change touches data, migrations or deploy scripts, or you're asked.
- Never close a milestone just to tidy up; it starts a release. Never publish a release, push a tag or publish to {{registry.name}} unless a human asked.
- Never build from an `idea`; shape it into `ready-*` tickets first.
- **These changes need explicit human approval first: {{approvals_line}}.** Propose the change and how to roll it back, then wait. Read-only lookups are fine.
- Never commit tokens, package-manager credentials (`.npmrc`, `settings.xml`, `gradle.properties`) or {{registry.name}} keys. Pipelines get secrets from {{secrets.ci_line}}; developers get them locally through {{secrets.local}}.
- Never run anything against a shared environment (databases, integration servers, clusters); agents use throwaway local or CI instances only. Deploys happen only through {{deploy.model_line}}.
